TEST 38479 -- ATMF - node provision
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-21/22, tb470
DUT:    x230-10GP (AW+ 5.5.5, awplus_5.5.5_2-20260918-7), console /dev/u0 @ 9600
Master: IE520 4-member VCStack, AMF node "IE520-stk", AMF master, backup media
        = USB in stack member 3
Network: AMF "tb470". The DUT is cabled to stack port1.0.2, which was used as
        the provisioning port -- no recabling was needed.

VERDICT: PASS

=========================== STEPS =========================================

STEP 1 -- "Create an AMF network Without the DUT"                      PASS
  The x230 was already a member from earlier work, so it was removed:
      x230(config)# no atmf network-name          <-- BARE form only
  ("no atmf network-name tb470" is rejected: % Invalid input.)
  Master then read Current ATMF Nodes 2 (IE520-stk + 4050-5g), DUT absent.

STEP 2 -- "Configure the AMF master for node provisioning. Create a profile
           for the DUT and create a config and add a release file"      PASS
      IE520-stk# atmf provision node x230-10GP
      IE520-stk[atmf-provision]# create
      ... locate ; copy flash:x230-default.cfg default.cfg
                 ; copy flash:x230-tb470.rel  x230-tb470.rel
      ... configure boot config default.cfg
      ... configure boot system x230-tb470.rel
  Verified:
      Node Name        : x230-10GP
      Provision Path   : usb:/atmf/tb470/nodes/x230-10GP/flash/
      Current boot image  : flash:/x230-tb470.rel (file exists)
      Current boot config : flash:/default.cfg   (file exists)

STEP 3 -- "Configure a switchport on the master for provisioning"       PASS
      IE520-stk(config)# interface port1.0.2
      IE520-stk(config-if)# atmf provision x230-10GP
  Verified by the provisioning marker in show atmf links:
      1.0.2  Downlink  Down  Init  *x230-10GP  -  Blocking
      * = Provisioned.
  NOTE: this assignment does NOT appear in "show running-config interface" --
  it lives in the AMF provisioning database. Check the asterisk, not the config.

STEP 4 -- "On the DUT use atmf cleanup"                                 PASS
  Ran on the x230 and completed -- flash wiped, node rebooted.
  **Contrast 38475:** the same command on the IE520 VCStack is refused with
  "% This command cannot be run when another stack member is present".
  atmf cleanup works on a STANDALONE node and not on a stack; this run is the
  positive half of that pair.

STEP 5 -- "Connect the DUT to the provisioning port on the master"      PASS
  Already cabled; the port had been shut to make the ATMF link inactive (see
  the ordering note below), so "connect" was performed as: no shutdown on
  stack port1.0.2.

STEP 6 -- "Boot the DUT. DUT should receive a configuration file and release
           file from the master"                                        PASS
  DUT console, times relative to the start of the capture:
      608.0s  atmffsd: Automatic node recovery started
      608.0s  atmffsd: Attempting to recover as x230-10GP
      653.1s  atmffsd: Checking controller and master node availability
      653.1s  atmffsd: Retrieving recovery data from recovery node IE520-stk
      689.1s  atmffsd: File recovery from master node succeeded. Node will now reboot
      765.2s  AlliedWare Plus (TM) v5.5.5
     1047.5s  Loading configuration file flash:/default.cfg, please wait.
     1054.5s  x230-10GP login:

  **THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE IS THE FLASH, NOT THE CONSOLE.** After provisioning,
  the DUT's flash -- which atmf cleanup had emptied -- holds BOTH files at the
  master profile's exact sizes and timestamps:
      25785296 -rw- Sep 21 2026 05:08:14  x230-tb470.rel
          1342 -rw- Sep 21 2026 04:59:16  default.cfg
  Those timestamps are the ones the files carry inside
  usb:/atmf/tb470/nodes/x230-10GP/flash/. Both files came from the master.
      Current boot config: flash:/default.cfg (file exists)
  The restored config is the x230's own (vlan 100, channel-group 1 on ports
  2 and 4), i.e. the content of default.cfg, applied.

=========================== TRAP: THE TFTP RED HERRING ====================

The DUT console shows, on EVERY boot including before any AMF activity:
      Loading tftp://10.38.215.1/x230-tb470.rel...
      Verifying release... OK
This x230's bootloader is configured to TFTP-boot its release from tb470, so
that line appears whether or not AMF delivered anything. **Do not read it as
"the release did not come from the master"** -- that was my first conclusion
and it was wrong. The flash listing above is what settles it.

=========================== ORDERING CONSTRAINTS ==========================

Three refusals, none documented in the case text, each of which stops the case
dead if you hit it in the wrong order:

 1. `configure boot config|system` -> "% Error: The provisioned node does not
    exist." while that node name is a LIVE AMF member. The DUT must be out of
    the network first -- which is exactly what the case's step 1 means by
    "Create an AMF network Without the DUT".
 2. `create` -> "% Error: A backup exists for this node. The backup must be
    deleted before this command is run." A node cannot be both backed-up and
    provisioned. Using `atmf backup now` to source a real config (which is
    otherwise a neat trick -- it writes the node's own config into the same
    path) therefore BLOCKS provisioning until you run
    `atmf backup delete <NODE-NAME>` (node name directly, no `node` keyword).
    Preserve the config elsewhere first; the delete removes the directory.
 3. `atmf provision <node>` on an interface -> "% Cannot provision an active
    ATMF link". The port must be idle. In the case this is implicit because
    the DUT is connected only at step 5; with the DUT already cabled, shut the
    port first.

=========================== OBSERVATIONS =================================

**The provisioned node does NOT rejoin the AMF network, and that is expected
here.** After the boot, the master's link to it holds steady at
      1.0.2  Downlink  Up  OneWay  *x230-10GP  0  Blocking
for 13+ minutes. Cause: the config we provisioned is the x230's own Aug-18
backup, which contains no `atmf network-name`. The node is provisioned and
running its delivered release and config, but is not an AMF member. Recorded
as a DECISION, per standing instruction: "the DUT received both files" and
"the DUT rejoined the network" are different claims, and this case asks only
for the former (step 6 wording). **Graded PASS on the case as written.** If a
future run wants the node to rejoin, provision a config containing
`atmf network-name tb470`.

**No loop, verified.** The restored config brought x230 port1.0.2 (to the
AR4050S) back up -- the shutdown I had applied lived in running-config only
and died with the wipe. That re-creates a stack/x230/4050 triangle with RSTP
disabled on all three devices. It is inert and was checked on every edge:
stack 1.0.2 ATMF state Blocking (not forwarding); stack loop-protection on
port1.0.2 reads Normal with no block; the AR4050S po1 shows its port1.0.2
"unsynchronized", so the x230 was not absorbed into that aggregate; no loop,
flap or topology events in the stack log.

=========================== HARNESS DEFECT (MINE) ========================

The step-6 capture used a flat observation window -- `end = time.time() + 1500`
with a 120 s sleep and no early exit. The case actually passed at **1054.5s**
(`x230-10GP login:`) and the script kept polling `show atmf links` every ~155 s
until ~2125s, printing the identical line six times. ~18 minutes of dead time,
and Terrence noticed the x230 does not take that long to boot.
**Wait for the CONDITION, not the clock** -- a `break` on `login:` in the DUT
stream would have closed it immediately. Same family as the flat
`mode(timeOut=1800)` bootloader trap already in memory.

